{
  "audio": "017.so-how-do.mp3",
  "paragraph": 17,
  "text": "So how do you keep context clean without mutating past turns? Start at the tool boundary. Imagine our agent runs the authentication test suite and triggers a massive stack trace. Dumping all of that raw text straight into context instantly drowns the model in noise. Instead, a well-built harness truncates terminal output down to a crisp forty-line summary, writes the full log to a temporary file on disk, and returns the file path so the agent can grep specific error lines only when needed.",
